
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

Run the hardware-independent cleaning command tests from PowerShell:
- `g++ -std=c++11 -Wall -Wextra -Werror -I src src/cleaning_command.cpp src/cleaning_phase.cpp test/test_cleaning_command/test_main.cpp -o cleaning_command_tests.exe`
- `.\cleaning_command_tests.exe`

ESP-NOW cleaning acknowledgements require the receiver to use the same
`cleaning.h` and `cleaning.cpp` files. Initialize ESP-NOW with the sender MAC
and register a handler on the receiver:

```cpp
bool applyCleaningCommand(const CleaningCommand &command)
{
  // Apply fan settings here. Return true only after they are applied.
  return true;
}

void setup()
{
  WiFi.mode(WIFI_STA);
  beginCleaningEspNow(SENDER_MAC);
  setCleaningCommandHandler(applyCleaningCommand);
}
```

The receiver acknowledges successfully applied commands automatically. The
sender retries up to three times and advances to phase 2 only after receiving
the matching acknowledgement.

RTC and EEPROM access is in `src/rtc_storage.h` and `src/rtc_storage.cpp`.
Call `beginRtcStorage()` once during setup, then use:
- `getRtcTimestamp()` to read the current `DDHHMM` timestamp.
- `saveDirtyMeasurements()` and `loadDirtyMeasurements()` for the 60 readings
  and six timestamps stored in EEPROM.
- `saveCleaningPhase()` and `loadCleaningPhase()` for the saved phase.
- `adjustRtcToBuildTime()` only when intentionally setting the DS3231 to the
  firmware build time.
